   "resumo_en": "Share the Land is the seventh studio album by Canadian rock band The Guess Who, released by RCA Records in October, 1970. It was their first album following the departure of Randy Bachman, and the band brought in two new guitarists, Kurt Winter and Greg Leskiw. The album was another international success for the band, reaching number seven in Canada and number fourteen in the US, and spawned three hit singles in the title track, \"Hand Me Down World\" and \"Hang On to Your Life\".",
